<%# §4.3 — "The modal also carries an optional, skippable thumbs prompt — 'would you
    make this again?' — answered with a single tap and written to `recipe.make_again`,
    the single canonical verdict for that recipe."

    Second step of the same dialog rather than a second dialog: the deduction is done
    and saved by the time this renders, so closing here costs nothing. That is what
    "optional, skippable" has to mean — Skip is a plain button that closes the dialog
    without a request, because leaving a verdict untouched is best done by not
    sending one. %>
<dialog data-controller="dialog" data-action="close->dialog#clear"
        class="m-auto w-11/12 max-w-md rounded-xl p-5 shadow-xl backdrop:bg-gray-900/40">
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Noted — <%= recipe_suggestion.title %></h2>
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-500">Your pantry is updated. Would you make it again?</p>

  <div class="mt-5 flex items-center justify-end gap-2">
    <button type="button" data-action="dialog#close"
            class="rounded-md px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-gray-500 hover:bg-gray-100 cursor-pointer">Skip</button>

    <%# Thumbs down: "the recipe joins the do-not-suggest list" and its card leaves the
        active view. Thumbs up marks it a favorite and badges every run it appears in. %>
    <%= button_to "👎 No", recipe_verdict_path(recipe_suggestion.recipe), method: :patch,
          params: { make_again: false },
          form_class: "inline",
          class: "rounded-md border border-gray-300 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-50 cursor-pointer" %>

    <%= button_to "👍 Yes", recipe_verdict_path(recipe_suggestion.recipe), method: :patch,
          params: { make_again: true },
          form_class: "inline",
          class: "rounded-md bg-amber-500 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:bg-amber-400 cursor-pointer" %>
  </div>
</dialog>
